{
  "dom_id": "step-q68126",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Jordan wants to paint the outside of his home. Using $2$ gallons of paint, he was able to paint $450$ square feet of the surface. There is a proportional relationship between the volume of paint $x$ (in gallons) that Jordan uses and the area $y$ (in square feet) he paints. What is the equation that represents the relationship between $x$ and $y?$",
  "worked_solution": "Every proportional relationship takes the form $y=kx,$ where $k$ is the constant of proportionality.\n\nWe are told that Jordan painted $y=450$ square feet using $x=2$ gallons of paint.\n\nWe can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-value to the $x$-value, as follows:\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{450}{2}=225\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation is\n\n$$\ny=225x.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
